\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation \n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\overset{^}{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7.5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $y=7.5+3x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-139643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "950c1ed7-f804-54f5-bf97-16bf2d1a663b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-41738/selection/33387a9c0fa3610b78bd774fa66b3a3379ba5675246c679d30d8b96bb7badcb7" :answer/id #uuid "4b50f6cc-5982-5757-b3f5-35019865b293" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2.5+3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41738/selection/c3f113c89454aa5e2fe6968b6bb72859fad0af8d22be63e4dff64c53499da1d6" :answer/id #uuid "0d60aee2-1192-5b5f-88ba-01cb66a78821" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=3-2.5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41738/selection/d447df7b701ac8d69b0d02e91f60af3194bcf24399b450fafb57a240c0920ec1" :answer/id #uuid "dfff1481-c209-56ab-81cd-e541eaaa6f0b" :an